Package: nutrigon
Title: Angular Separation Between Nutritional Optima in the Geometric
        Framework for Nutrition
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Juliano", "Morimoto", email = "juliano.morimoto@abdn.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits quadratic response surfaces to trait data collected under the
    Geometric Framework for Nutrition and computes the angular separation
    (theta) between the nutritional optima of two traits, with bootstrap
    confidence intervals. Provides a simulation-based per-result reliability
    diagnostic that compares a given result's risk-factor profile (curvature
    elongation, distance to the angular boundary of the design, and angular
    separation) against a pre-built validation grid of configurations with
    known ground-truth bootstrap coverage. Includes the Lee et al. (2008)
    Drosophila lifespan/fecundity dataset as a worked example.
